course: dictionary
lesson: 3903
title: What friendship means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Friendship is the bond between friends: you like each other, you trust each other, and you enjoy spending time together. «Sharing silly jokes, like knock-knock jokes, builds friendship and helps younger children learn language.» The words around friendship show it grows when you do things together.
explain: Friendship also means feeling friendly and kind to someone. The clues show what that looks like: sharing, listening, keeping promises and saying sorry. «Some friendships start slowly; don't give up in the first week.» Slowly tells you a friendship can take time to grow.
explain: Friendships can change. You can make a friendship, start one, or end one. «Friendships last a lifetime when people keep showing up for each other.» Keep showing up is the clue: a friendship lasts because people keep caring and turning up for each other.
fact: Friendship is a noun: a friendship, friendships.
fact: Friendship means the relationship between friends, and also the feeling of being friendly and kind to someone.
fact: Good friendships are fair. True friends do not make you feel bad or pressure you into unsafe things.
fact: Phrases you may see are «a close friendship», «make a friendship», «friendship bracelet» and «friendship group».
fact: In stories like «Charlotte's Web», friendship is a big theme: Charlotte and Wilbur look after each other.
exercise: Which of these is a sign of good friendship? | Taking everything without asking | *Sharing and keeping promises | Making your friend feel bad | Pressuring a friend into unsafe things
exercise: «Some friendships start slowly; don't give up in the first week.» What does this sentence suggest? | *A friendship can take time to grow | Friendships never change | Friends should be made in one day | Give up on new friends quickly
exercise: In «Charlotte's Web», what is a big theme? | *Friendship between Charlotte and Wilbur | Cooking a big dinner | Living on the moon | Racing cars
test: Which phrase means a group of friends who spend time together? | start a friendship | end a friendship | *friendship group | friendship bracelet
test: «Being beaten by a friend can be fun, and asking people to play is how many friendships start.» What is one way a friendship can start? | Shout at people to go away | Never speak to anyone | *Ask people to play | Ignore everyone in the playground
exam: Which word is the plural of friendship? | friendshipping | friendship | *friendships | friendshipy
